    },
    {
      "image": "videos/08-great-filter/3.jpg",
      "seconds": 28.93,
      "text": "Robin Hanson's answer was a filter. Somewhere on the path from dead chemistry to a galactic civilization, there is a step almost nothing survives. And the question that matters is where it sits. If the filter is behind us, in the leap to complex life, then we are extraordinarily lucky and extraordinarily alone. If it sits ahead of us, then every silent star is a civilization that already reached our stage, and did not pass.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 8,
        "pitch": -1
      },
      "clips": [
        {
          "src": "videos/08-great-filter/v3-1.mp3",
